* {{IPA|en|/ˈɑm.lət/|/ˈɑm.lɪt/|/ˈɑ.mə.lət/|a=US,Canada}}
* {{audio|en|en-ca-omelette.opus|a=CA}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# A dish made with beaten [[egg]]s cooked in a frying pan without stirring, flipped over to cook on both sides, and sometimes filled or topped with other foodstuffs, for example cheese or chives.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:Marjorie Bowen]] [pseudonym; Margaret Gabrielle Vere Long]|chapter=The Heretic|title=The Quest of Glory|location=London|publisher=[[w:Methuen Publishing|Methuen & Co. Ltd.]]{{nb...|36 Essex Street W.C.}}|year=1912|section=part I (The Quest Joyful)|pages=69–70|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/questofglory00boweuoft/page/70/mode/1up|passage=He crossed to the window, which looked on to a herb garden, and seated himself on the chintz-covered window-seat and delicately watched the two, who were engaged in eating '''omelette''' and salad at a round table near the fire-place.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=[[w:J. B. Priestley|J[ohn] B[oynton] Priestley]]|chapter=London End|title=The Image Men|location=Boston, Mass.|publisher=w:Little, Brown and Company|year=1969|page=288|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/imagemen00prie/page/288/mode/1up|lccn=69-15075|passage=She had never meant to confide in him — certainly not here, eating '''omelette''' and cheese sauce — but that look seemed to demand a confidence.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Christine Pullein-Thompson|title=Wait for Me Phantom horse|location=London|publisher=Award Publications Limited|year=1985|year_published=1997|page=64|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/waitformephantom0000pull/page/64/mode/1up|isbn=0-86163-845-X|passage=She stayed to lunch that day, eating '''omelette''' and peas in the kitchen, followed by treacle tart.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} A form of [[shellcode]] that searches the [[address space]] for multiple small blocks of data ("eggs") and [[recombine]]s them into a larger block to be [[execute]]d.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2015|author=Herbert Bos; Fabian Monrose; Gregory Blanc|title=Research in Attacks, Intrusions, and Defenses: 18th International Symposium
|passage=This approach would be altered for an optimal '''omelette''' based exploit. One would spray the heap with the '''omelette''' code solely, then load a single copy of the additional shellcode eggs into memory outside the target region for the spray.}}

